# Trivy exceptions. Every entry is narrow (one advisory id), carries a
# reason, and EXPIRES: once the date passes Trivy reports it again and the
# CI gate fails, forcing a re-check instead of a permanent silence.

# tzdata 2026b in the gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot base image.
# DLA-4792-1 is a timezone-rules data update (2026c), not a code
# vulnerability; Trivy rates it UNKNOWN, which ci.yml's PR scan treats as
# blocking. As of 2026-10-07 the newest upstream distroless image
# (sha256:afa5c872…) still ships 2026b, so there is no base to move to yet.
# Drop this line once a rebuilt distroless image carries 2026c.
DLA-4792-1 exp:2026-11-07

# DLA-4845-1: ca-certificates 20250419~deb12u1 → deb12u2 (removes the
# distrusted Comodo "AAA Certificate Services" and "emSign ECC Root CA - G3"
# roots). gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot does not yet ship the
# fixed package; the latest upstream image still carries deb12u1 (checked
# 2026-10-21). The exposure itself is closed: the Dockerfile copies the
# bookworm builder's deb12u2 bundle over distroless's
# /etc/ssl/certs/ca-certificates.crt (150 → 148 certs). Trivy still reports
# the finding only because it reads distroless's dpkg status metadata. The
# expiry forces a re-check: remove this entry and the COPY once distroless
# ships deb12u2. Same fix as iam-delegation ed2f405.
DLA-4845-1 exp:2026-11-21

# DLA-4854-1: tzdata 2026b-0+deb12u1 → 2026e-0+deb12u1, a timezone-database
# refresh (Trivy: UNKNOWN; the CI gate fails on UNKNOWN). Same package and
# situation as DLA-4792-1 above.
# Not exploitable here: the service never loads a zone (no time.LoadLocation, no
# time/tzdata, no time.Local use; all timestamps are UTC).
# Blocked upstream: on 2026-10-26 the newest gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12
# :nonroot digest (sha256:afa5c872…) still ships tzdata 2026b. Remove this
# entry and re-pin once distroless ships tzdata >= 2026e.
DLA-4854-1 exp:2026-11-30

# DLA-4867-1: tzdata 2026b-0+deb12u1 → 2026f-0+deb12u1, a further
# timezone-database refresh in the same chain as DLA-4792-1 / DLA-4854-1
# (Trivy: UNKNOWN; the CI gate fails on UNKNOWN). Same package and situation:
# gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot (sha256:afa5c872…) still ships
# tzdata 2026b as of 2026-10-30. Not exploitable: the service never calls
# time.LoadLocation, imports time/tzdata, or reads time.Local — all
# timestamps are UTC. Remove once distroless ships tzdata >= 2026f.
DLA-4867-1 exp:2026-12-07

# GO-2026-5932: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and unsafe by
# design. The "fix" recorded in the advisory is a pre-release pseudo-version
# (v0.58.1-0.20261009181718-2f1f834330b2) that has never been tagged as a
# stable release and cannot be pinned in a module that uses go get / GOPROXY
# without side-effects. This service does NOT import x/crypto/openpgp directly;
# the dependency is transitive (via platform-gincommon / OpenBao SDK).
# govulncheck v1.x confirms our code does not call any vulnerable symbol:
#   "Your code is affected by 0 vulnerabilities."
# Trivy reports it because --ignore-unfixed sees the pseudo-version as "fixed"
# and the local Trivy DB was stale when the pre-push gate ran (CI always pulls
# a fresh DB, hence the CI failure). This entry is intentionally short-lived:
# when x/crypto cuts a stable release >= v0.59.0 that includes the openpgp
# removal, upgrade x/crypto and drop this line.
GO-2026-5932 exp:2027-02-05
